# === Generated skill outputs (do not commit) ===

# reviewing-code: review artifact written to the repo root
REVIEW.md
# RM-003 pass 5: committed event-stream fixture replays reviewing-code's real
# output name (REVIEW.md); re-include the fixture copy (the rule above is
# basename-wide).
!skills/authoring-skills/evals/fixtures/event-streams/**/REVIEW.md

# Runtime-generated plans/agents when this library is consumed, or when the
# free-tier council agent defs dropped in (designing-architecture,
# FREE-TIER-COUNCIL). In THIS repo the plans directory is the deliberate
# opt-in exception (2026-09-23, ADR-0008): .opencode/plans/ is the library's
# own construction record (plans + archived session handoffs) and IS tracked;
# the plan-format default (runtime artifacts, not committed) stays in force
# for consumer repos. Runtime noise under .opencode/ (node_modules, package
# manifests) stays ignored everywhere.
# Contents-level ignore (.opencode/*, not .opencode/) because gitignore
# cannot re-include a file under an excluded parent directory.
.opencode/*
# Eval fixtures legitimately embed an .opencode/ project layout (the
# workdir must look like a project for the eval prompt); un-ignore inside
# skill eval fixtures only:
!skills/*/evals/fixtures/**/.opencode/
!skills/*/evals/fixtures/**/.opencode/**
# The library's own working-artifact tier (rm-003.md flagged the
# untracked-ledger problem):
!.opencode/plans/
!.opencode/plans/**

# === Run telemetry (observing-runs / RM-001) — never commit ===
# JSONL run logs are git-ignored so per-run telemetry is never committed;
# aggregates persist out-of-band (RM-003/009/011), raw lines are pruned.
logs/

# === OS / tooling noise ===
.DS_Store
*.log
node_modules/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# === Local agent scratch (must stay inside the repo worktree; never /tmp) ===
.scratch/

# Playwright installed into the capturing-ui-evidence skill dir per its
# SKILL.md bootstrap (the installed skill is a symlink here) — environment
# artifact, not library content.
skills/capturing-ui-evidence/package*.json

# === Deprecated docs (removed from the repo; never track) ===
PLAN.md
# docs/handoffs/ retired again 2026-09-23 (ADR-0008): session-boundary
# handoffs are working artifacts whose durable essence is extracted into
# tracked docs (ADRs / AGENTS.md / ROADMAP) before merge; the working-artifact
# tier is .opencode/plans/ (tracked in this repo, see the .opencode/ entry).
docs/handoffs/
